**EXERCISE 4.20.** For approximable $f, g : D \to D$ prove that

$$\mathrm{fix}(f \circ g) = f(\mathrm{fix}(g \circ f)).$$

The development is with the
[Fix of a composite](1980_fixComp.md) peer.

<!-- formalization -->

**Theorem (`example_420`).** For approximable $f,g$, $\\mathrm{fix}(f\\circ g)=f(\\mathrm{fix}(g\\circ f))$.

*Proof.* Apply the composite fixed-point commutation law. ∎
